      "writtenOn": "2022-11-29T15:39:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "PCI noobie question: what are we\u0027re doing exactly here? The kernel docs say\n```\nranges:\n  description:\n    As described in IEEE Std 1275-1994, but must provide at least a\n    definition of non-prefetchable memory. One or both of prefetchable Memory\n    and IO Space may also be provided.\n```\nso the entries in `ranges` have different meanings (unlike say entries in `/memory`) and are distinguished based on their `bus_address` top bits (flags) but we seem to be selecting whichever range that has the largest `size` as our PCI memory irrespective of whether it\u0027s prefetchable, non-prefetchable, or IO?",
      "range": {
